From: CB1 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Native PGS bitmap controls with explicit subtitle authoring

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Position/zoom and linear saturation/PQ equations adapted from avdvplus/xbmc
e0614d7a6713369bbcfe42152223f1cdaec3dbf1, OverlayRenderer.cpp and
system/shaders/GLES/2.0/gles_shader_texture_noblend.frag (GPL-2.0-or-later).
Original Team Kodi / Team XBMC notices are retained in the native helper.
No skin, VS10, GUI shader pipeline or movie reconstruction is imported.

Use native video/screen rectangles, existing bitmap texture caching and
premultiplication. Neutral settings bypass all new colour/geometry math.
Authoring overrides require track reselection/reopen to decode the original
YCbCr palette with the right matrix; never reinterpret already-clipped RGB.
Depends on ffmpeg-9900-08-pgs-authoring.patch for explicit decoder matrices.
Disc menu source comes from native callbacks, never a second menu engine.

